{
	"title": "a walk through a folder of processes reads only what it steps on [the hedgehog's wall 2, 10-28: chee \"we need a fine grained way of looking at the thing we care about, and only change if it changes\"]: a memo reading /nb/a/v, a's memo, is not run again when another process starts or stops in /nb, nor when a plain node is made there; a's memo changing runs it",
